    "chunk_size_bytes": 1776,
    "chunk_text": "Hon. Chairman, since that matter relating to the Department of Archaeology was raised a while ago, I would like to say that I also have certain comments to make. I think I will take it up during the Discussion on the Votes of the Ministry of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs. It is pertaining to an important religious place of worship for the Muslims for several centuries - \"Daftar Jailani\" in Balangoda - which has unnecessarily been desecrated due to intervention by the Urban Development Authority over a period of time. Now, several new structures have come up. That is beside the point. However, the areas occupied by Muslims are now being seriously hampered due to unnecessary intervention\n\nAccording to the Minister, the Urban Development Authority has identified 10 cities around the Island and also the Hon. President, in his Speech, referred to Jaffna, Eheliyagoda, Batticaloa, Chilaw and Matara and I do not know what other cities come under those ten cities. In fact, I represent Kandy, which is the second largest city in this country and the most important, sacred city for Buddhists, and there, several areas particularly need to be addressed when it comes to urban regeneration projects, especially for underserved settlements, where people live in tenements with less facilities. There are several such areas like Mahaiyawa, Katukele and Deiyannewela.\n\nFor instance, if we take Katukele, our young athlete Fathima Shafiya Yamick, whom we all praise for the big achievement by winning three gold medals and shattering three records including the 28-year old record of P.T. Usha, comes from those tenements, a very underserved settlement in Kandy. Sir, I record my appreciation for her wonderful achievement. All of us are very proud about of her."
  },
