    "chunk_text": ",\u0d82\u0dc0\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dbb ,\u0dc3\u0db1 \u0d9a \u0dcf \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0db1\u0db4\u0d9a\u0dca\u0da7 \u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dc0 \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dab\u0dba \u0db4\u0d9a\u0dca \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dba \u0db4\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1 \u0d95\u0db1\u0dd1.\u0dbd\u0dda \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dc1\u0dca\u0dda\u0dc2\u0db4\u0dba \u0db4\u0db1\u0dca\u0db8\u0dc0 \u0db1\u0dc3 \u0db4\u0d9f\u0db1\u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dbb \u0dca\u0dc5\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0da7 \u0dc0\u0dc3\u0dc4\u0dd2 \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dd3\u0db4\u0d89\u0daf\u0dd3 \u0db4\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dc1\u0dca\u0db1\u0db1 \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dca\u0dba \u0db4\u0d9a\u0da7 \u0db8\u0dd4\u0dc4\u0dd4\u0dab \u0db4\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1 \u0dc3\u0dd2\u0dd4 \u0db4\u0dc0\u0dd3\u0dcf \u0dd2\u0db6\u0db4\u0db6\u0db1\u0dc0\u0dcf.\u0dbd\u0dda In Kalmunai area, Sir, the Kittange pump house and the surrounding areas always go under water. Regarding that also, there was a plan under the earlier project called Climate Resilience Improvement Project - CRIP. It had been in operation, but had been wound up. They had proposed a balloon dam near the Kallar Bridge to stop water from going into the sea. Since sand banks are formed, they proposed a deflatable dam so that when the water level rises, they could deflate the dam and allow the water to flow into the sea. So, that was a plan that had been submitted, but nothing had happened so far. The CRIP had suddenly been wound up and still, the Kittange pump house is unable to cope with the flood situation and therefore, that has to be implemented.\n\nTogether with that, my Friend, the Hon. M. S. Abthul Wazeeth mentioned about the problems in his area. Particularly when it comes to water supply for the Pottuvil area, it is an imperative necessity today to have the Heda Oya Reservoir Project started because that reservoir is important, both for irrigation and water supply. Unfortunately, because of some objections from the farmers of Siyambalanduwa, that is not happening. We know that several other projects nearby have already been approved, but this Heda Oya Project, we have been making efforts for several long years to start. I hope the Hon. Minister in charge of water supply would speak to the irrigation authorities and try to start work on the Heda\n\n1587 1588\n\n[,\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dd2\u0db6 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc6\u0db1 \u0dc4\u0d9a\u0dd3\u0dda \u0db8\u0dc0\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0db4\u0db1\u0dca\u0dc0\u0dc3\u0dda\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 24\n\nOya Project. Of course, we will need some funding from abroad with the current debt situation in the country. So, to have the Heda Oya Project prioritized, it would be important to have discussions with the ERD so that you could start it."
  },
