    "chunk_size_bytes": 1491,
    "chunk_text": "Commission\u2019s recommendations and I remember speaking during Budgets, supporting a lot of what you said. Unfortunately, since this Government came into power, certain revisions have been made, but, I think, they fall grossly short of the Subodhini Salary Commission's recommendations.\n\nI will give you just one example. If you take Grade 2-II teachers, the shortfall between the Subodhini Committee and your Government\u2019s recommendations for 2025 was Rs. 10, 489, for 2026, it will be Rs. 12, 879 and for 2027, it will be Rs. 15, 270. That is a lot of money, that is a hell of a lot of money! I have a whole list of shortfalls and I will table* it. I think you must rectify that.\n\nAnother complaint I get and the severe criticism that comes now, Hon. Prime Minister, is - the Ranil Wickremesinghe Government, in order to get funding from the Asian Development Bank, went through a process of unilaterally creating reforms, which was heavily opposed, including by the JVP and yourself; we opposed it as well - that it is more or less the same reforms that are being pushed by this Government. The question is, just for the sake of getting funds of the ADB, are we going to push for those reforms, which were made unilaterally and without any serious consultation with the stakeholders, through your Government? I do not think you should take that blame; I think you should look into that.\n\nHon. Prime Minister, with the school time being extended - I want to mention this - particularly the"
