    "chunk_size_bytes": 2111,
    "chunk_text": "Then, Hon. Prime Minister, I would like to take up the matter of teachers serving in difficult areas. If you take Jaffna, the difficult schools have been revised; those have been revised on certain criteria, which, in a place like Jaffna, make no sense. Sixteen schools in the islands in Jaffna have been taken off this list of difficult areas simply because those areas have, for example, a post office, a hospital or something to that effect. But if you take those islands, Hon. Prime Minister, transportation is the biggest problem there. Having a hospital, a bank or a post office being the reason for those schools to be taken off that list of difficult areas makes no sense because the teachers who come from the mainland face that same problem of transportation. So, again, taking 16 schools off that list, I think, does not make sense; it just does not make sense. I can go through a whole list of schools in the Northern Province and the Eastern Province which have the same problem. Therefore, that criteria is just irrelevant for our areas.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0db1\u0db4\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbd\u0db8\u0dca \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9c\u0bc0.\u0b9c\u0bc0. \u0ba4\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0ba9\u0bae\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. G.G. Ponnambalam) Hon. Presiding Member, I have spoken for only nine minutes.\n\n1869 1870\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014 * \u0db4\u0dd4\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dad\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0db1\u0d9a \u0dad\u0db6\u0dcf \u0d87\u0dad. * \u0ba8\u0bc2\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bae\u0bb2\u0bc8\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0bae\u0bb5\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0bb3\u0ba4\u0bc1. * Placed in the Library.\n\n\u0dd9\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dda\u0dca \u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc0\n\ntoday\u2019s context, is insufficient. In Parliament - you have cut down a lot of the perks - one day\u2019s meal is Rs. 1,500! So, can you imagine getting an allowance of Rs. 1,500 for the whole month? I think, again, there is something wrong; blatantly, there is something wrong. Especially, if you are trying to encourage teachers to go out into difficult areas, this discourages them, making sure that they choose something else other than going and serving there. So, Hon. Prime Minister, under those circumstances, I urge you to look into those matters."
