    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc0\u0d86\u0dad\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba) \u0d91\u0db8\u0dca.\u0d91\u0dda.\u0d92.\u0d91\u0db8\u0dca. \u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dda\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc4\u0db1 \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0b8e\u0bae\u0bcd.\u0b8e\u0bb2\u0bcd.\u0b8f.\u0b8e\u0bae\u0bcd. \u0bb9\u0bbf\u0bb8\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb2\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb9\u0bcd) (The Hon. (Dr.) M.L.A.M. Hizbullah) Sir, I had seven minutes. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0dd9\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bae\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bc8\u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) No, you have only six minutes. [4.30 p.m.]\n\nHon. Presiding Member, I rise today to contribute to this Discussion on the Votes of the Ministry of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education. At the outset, I wish to express my sincere appreciation to the Hon. Prime Minister and Minister of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education, her two Deputy Ministers, the Secretary and other officials of that Ministry for the dedicated work carried out despite economic limitations and many structural challenges. The steps already taken to stabilize the education system, strengthen teacher recruitment and introduce digital learning initiatives are commendable and deserve recognition.\n\nHon. Prime Minister, our school curriculum must evolve with the changing needs of the 21st Century. The world has moved beyond memorization-based learning. Today\u2019s children need critical thinking, creativity, financial literacy, environmental awareness, STEM skills and technology literacy. I appreciate the Ministry\u2019s efforts to begin updating the curriculum, but we must accelerate these reforms so that every student gains the skills needed for future jobs and global competitiveness.\n\nSir, I acknowledge the progress in introducing smart classrooms, digitized textbooks and online learning platforms. However, the digital divide still affects thousands of students, especially in rural districts. Strengthening ICT education, computer labs, AI literacy and mathematics instruction is essential. No child must be left behind simply because they lack a device or Internet access."
  },
