    "chunk_size_bytes": 1241,
    "chunk_text": "\u0dd9\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0daf\u0db4\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbd\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9c\u0bc0.\u0b9c\u0bc0. \u0ba4\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0ba9\u0bae\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. G.G. Ponnambalam) Hon. Speaker, you would recall that at the Party Leaders' Meeting, the request was made whether the Vote on the 05th could be postponed, if necessary, to discuss the current tragic situation the country is facing, that particularly with regard to taking policy decisions, Parliament must convene. We asked the Government to consider allowing three days, including today and tomorrow, for us to have discussions with regard to the current situation. The Government said that they cannot postpone the Vote on the 05th.\n\nThe officials of the other districts of the Northern Province managed to come to the meeting, actually, unofficially. I mentioned this at the Party Leaders' Meeting. Therefore, we asked the Government to allows us to discuss the prevailing situation, at least, today and tomorrow and that we will pass the Budget without any debate on the 05th, but the Government refused to do that. The Government refused to do that and only allowed us to discuss the prevailing situation till 12.30 p.m. today. What is the point in doing that?"
  },
  {
